{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMfprGKspUX7cqLM7Zva","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011o8yrDZCinGbUtzzdgv6YU","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"cases":[{"id":"auth_boundary","met":true,"report_quote":"The auth gate itself is sound. `app.use('/mcp', …)` runs before every route under `/mcp`, including `/mcp/init`.","reason":"Correctly says the gateway middleware precedes all /mcp routes. It makes no unauthenticated-attack claim and no OAuth audience claim."},{"id":"runtime_scope","met":true,"report_quote":"**Out of scope, per the README:** the `createTransport` implementation, the gateway and secret store, framing limits, audit, and process supervision. I didn't assess any of these.","reason":"Makes no runtime test, crash, deployed-secret or host-audit claim. Leaves the external controls unassessed."},{"id":"safe_session_and_errors","met":true,"report_quote":"The `route` wrapper correctly sends async failures to `next`, so there are no unhandled rejections.","reason":"Recognizes the rejection forwarding. Says the session ID is only a lookup key and does not allege an inherited-key defect."},{"id":"coverage_get","met":false,"report_quote":"","reason":"GET /mcp is never assessed on its own. There is only a generic remark about the lookup key and the wrapper, with no GET-specific analysis or ledger entry."},{"id":"coverage_delete","met":true,"report_quote":"`DELETE /mcp` passes the request to the transport but never calls `sessions.delete(id)`.","reason":"Assesses the DELETE handler's behavior with line evidence (routes.mjs:21-25). Also covers its use of the error wrapper."},{"id":"coverage_launch","met":false,"report_quote":"","reason":"launch.json is never resolved or discussed. The report only separates the createTransport implementation as out of scope."},{"id":"coverage_create","met":true,"report_quote":"`POST /mcp/init` has no cap and no expiry, so memory grows without bound.